# SLIC Individual — Light

MATLAB scripts for individual whole-brain parcellation of resting-state fMRI data with normalized cuts and simple linear iterative clustering.

[GPL-3.0 license](LICENSE) · [Manuscript](manuscript.pdf)

The original documentation describes this as a version of [SLIC-individual](https://github.com/yuzhounh/SLIC-individual) with lower memory use in weight-matrix and Dice-coefficient calculations.

## Quick Start

1. Open the repository directory in MATLAB with Parallel Computing Toolbox available.
2. Review [m1_download.m](m1_download.m). It expects `NIfTI_20140122.zip` and `SLIC_individual_data.zip`; it attempts to download missing archives from the URLs in that file. These historical download endpoints have not been checked here.
3. Review the data preparation and worker counts before running the full workflow. [m1_prepare.m](m1_prepare.m) selects subjects 00440, 01018, and 01244, and cluster counts from 50 to 1000 in steps of 50. [m1_parc.m](m1_parc.m) requests three parallel workers.
4. Run from the repository directory:

```matlab
m1_main
```

Preparation extracts the dataset, decompresses root-level `*.gz` files, removes those compressed files, and moves the subject images into `data/`. Use a dedicated copy of the repository for the demo.

## Workflow and Evaluation

The entry point downloads inputs, prepares data, runs parcellation, draws illustrations, computes evaluation metrics, and summarizes and plots the results.

The documented comparisons cover cluster counts, spatial discontiguity, functional homogeneity, and reproducibility. When adapting the scripts to another dataset, review the number of redundant eigenvectors as described in the original notes.

## Repository Structure

- [m1_main.m](m1_main.m): full workflow.
- [m1_download.m](m1_download.m) and [m1_prepare.m](m1_prepare.m): dependencies and dataset preparation.
- [m1_parc.m](m1_parc.m): parcellation stages.
- [Ncut_sub_parc.m](Ncut_sub_parc.m) and [SLIC_sub_parc.m](SLIC_sub_parc.m): subject-level methods.
- [m1_eval.m](m1_eval.m), [m1_summ.m](m1_summ.m), and [m1_plot.m](m1_plot.m): evaluation and reporting.
- [manuscript.pdf](manuscript.pdf): accompanying paper.

## Related Projects

- [SLIC-individual](https://github.com/yuzhounh/SLIC-individual): related implementation identified by the original documentation.

